-- A video element playing the test image (a stream captured from a canvas
-- holding it, each pixel an 8×8 block), its current frame copied
-- whole into an `rgba8unorm` texture whose blocks' centres are read back
-- (docs/design/webgpu.md §8, §10's S5 acceptance; ledger §6). The image is
-- the 8×8 test image of four opaque quadrants whose bytes
-- `GpuMedia.colour` writes out by hand; every pixel read back is compared
-- with those bytes, never with anything the code under test computed. The
-- gates' fake host keeps no texels, so its transcript reads zeros;
-- `test-webgpu`'s is the GPU's (`_expected.webgpu-expected`).
-- A video frame passes through the host's YUV conversion, so each byte may
-- differ by up to 12 from the image's (a tolerance far below the distance
-- between any two quadrant colours).
import GpuMedia
import GpuPage
import Tea


run : ⊤ → List String
run ⊤ = GpuMedia.copiedVideo 12


main : Tea.Program
main = GpuPage.program [ ( "run", run ) ]
